### Tracker formula pattern

```excel
G3  =IFERROR(INDEX(TrackerData!$A$2:$A$106,MATCH($B$3,TrackerData!$B$2:$B$106,0)),"")
item cell =IFERROR(IF(INDEX('Item Pivot'!$G$5:$G$1474,MATCH($G$3&"|"&$A14,'Item Pivot'!$A$5:$A$1474,0))="",NA(),
                     INDEX('Item Pivot'!$G$5:$G$1474,MATCH($G$3&"|"&$A14,'Item Pivot'!$A$5:$A$1474,0))),NA())
```

`NA()` rather than `""` keeps missing sessions out of the line charts; an empty string would plot as 0. The conditional formats on the % block read the raw-level block (`LEFT(x,2)="1/"` → red; numerator = denominator → green). Charts use `from_rows=True`, `display_blanks="gap"` and `visible_cells_only=False`, because column A is hidden.

