## 7. Trend and flag logic

Sessions are **not comparable on raw %**. S1 has 7 items, S2 excludes scaling, and S3 is a scaling-only practice test with a mean of 59%. So individual trends use the **within-session z-score**: (student Equal % − session mean) ÷ session SD.

- **Trend** = slope of z across the scored sessions (needs ≥ 3).
- **Change** = latest z − mean of earlier z (needs ≥ 3).

`PE_FLAG_CONFIG` (edit, or pass `flagConfig={...}`):

| Key | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `lowPercentile` | 0.15 | "Low" = at or below the 15th percentile of that session |
| `minLowSessions` | 2 | **RED**: low in ≥ 2 marked sessions |
| `safetyMinCount` | 1 | **RED**: bottom level on Infection control ("No mask or gloves…") or Instrument use ("Dangerous") |
| `damageRedSessions` | 2 | **RED**: Major damage in ≥ 2 sessions; **AMBER** once, only if it was in the latest session |
| `missRed` | 2 | **RED**: no scored form for ≥ 2 marked sessions; AMBER for 1 |
| — | — | **RED**: no PE forms at all (3 students: Ang, Gupta, Molon — check enrolment) |
| `declineZ` | −0.75 | **AMBER**: change in z ≤ −0.75 |
| `latestGrMax` | 2 | **AMBER**: latest GR ≤ 2 |
| `latestPrMax` | 1 | **AMBER**: latest Readiness = 1 |
| `selfGapPts` / `minSelfSessions` | 15 / 2 | **AMBER**: self ≥ 15 pts above the assessor on average |
| (single low session) | — | **AMBER** only when it is the **latest** session |

Tuning history: the first pass flagged 55 RED + 21 AMBER, because any Major damage counted as a safety event. Major damage is 12–17% per session on the typodont, so it was noise. The second pass gave 27 RED + 56 AMBER, driven by single-session lows. The final settings give **27 RED + 18 AMBER**.

