## 10. Design decisions

- **Excel, not HTML:** it matches the coordinators' existing flagging workbooks, and they can filter and annotate it.
- **One Tracker sheet with a dropdown** instead of 105 per-student sheets. It keeps the file small (≈ 275 KB) and gives one place to look. The per-student data is still all visible, statically, on Item Pivot.
- **Four section charts instead of one 14-line chart:** 14 lines, many sitting at 100%, were unreadable. Within a section, lines use one colour family plus different dash styles.
- **Canonical item ids** (`PE_ITEMS`) keyed on the **criterion name**, not the MC number. The same criterion has different MC numbers across sessions (PE-03 MC1 = debridement incisor; PE-05 MC1 = seating).
- **Relative colour scale** on the grid, because absolute % would paint all of S3 red.
- **Nothing written to Postgres;** this reads the JSON only.

